  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reception and Inclusion of People Fleeing the Conflict in Ukraine to Slovakia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the beginning of the recent conflict in Ukraine on 24 February 2022, substantive flows and displacements across Ukraine and toward neighbouring countries have been reported. Hundreds of thousands of people have been forced to flee their homes in search of safety. Before the conflict the usual average of entry to Slovakia from Ukraine was 1,444 persons per day. Since the 24th of February there has been a tenfold increase in arrivals. Besides Third Country Nationals (TCN) who represent around 12 per cent of persons, there are mainly Ukrainian women with children, elderly and unaccompanied minors crossing the Slovak border as Ukraine has announced mobilization of men between 18 and 60 years old. The overall objective of this project is to ensure the immediate support to conflict-affected individuals at the Slovak-Ukrainian border and support the inclusion of the Ukrainian nationals, TCNs and migrants who fled the country to Slovakia.</narrative>
  </description>
